[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=SCIM Input Method
GenericName=Input Method
Comment=Smart Common Input Method, as the compositor's input method
Exec=@SCIM_LIBEXECDIR@/scim-launcher -c socket -e socket -f wayland
Icon=scim
Terminal=false
NoDisplay=true
X-KDE-Wayland-VirtualKeyboard=true
# Offers scim to KWin as the session's input method, selectable under
# System Settings -> Keyboard -> Virtual Keyboard.
#
# wayland.so speaks both input-method protocol generations and binds whichever
# the compositor offers, so this entry needs no per-desktop knowledge: KWin gets
# input-method-v1, a wlroots compositor would get v2.
#
# The input method has to be launched by KWin: it hands out zwp_input_method_v1
# only to the process it started for this role, so the autostart entry
# (scim.desktop) cannot obtain it.
# The launcher is exec'd directly rather than through "scim -f wayland": KWin
# hands the input method a pre-connected wayland fd in WAYLAND_SOCKET, and the
# wrapper would fork and exec a second time, after which the fd is no longer
# there to inherit. -c socket -e socket adopts the warm backend that scim -d
# supervises instead of loading every engine again.
